-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/60174a52-d709-45e2-a84b-8c2a91e9ba32
-- title:
--   Theorem 4.2 — PLIAG converges linearly: $\Gamma_\alpha(x_k)\le(1+\alpha\mu)^{-k}\Gamma_\alpha(x_0)$
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $w$ is a Legendre function with constraint set $\mathcal Q=\overline{\operatorname{dom}w}$, $h$ is proper, lower semicontinuous and convex, the optimal solution set $\mathcal X$ of (1.1) is nonempty and compact, every block $\mathcal J_k$ is nonempty and every delay satisfies $\tau_k^n\le\tau$ (assumption A0).
--
--   Assume B1–B4 with constants $L_n$ and $\mu$ and function $\ell$ ($\ell$ monotonically increasing with $\ell(1)=1$; the B4 inequality when $\tau>0$). Let $L=\max_{k\ge0}\sum_{j\in\mathcal J_k}L_j$ and let $\{x_k\}$ be generated by the PLIAG method with a constant step size $\alpha$ satisfying
--
--   $$
--   0<\alpha\le\alpha_0:=\frac{\big(1+\frac{\mu}{L}\frac1{\ell(\tau+1)}\big)^{\frac1{\tau+1}}-1}{\mu}. \tag{4.5}
--   $$
--
--   Let $\Gamma_\alpha(x)=\Phi(x)-\Phi^*+\frac1\alpha\inf_{z\in\mathcal X}D_w(z,x)$ be the Lyapunov function (4.6).
--   Then:
--
--   1. (linear convergence of the Lyapunov function) for every $k\ge0$,
--   $$
--   \Gamma_\alpha(x_k)\le\Big(\frac{1}{1+\alpha\mu}\Big)^k\Gamma_\alpha(x_0); \tag{4.7}
--   $$
--   2. (function values) for every $k\ge0$,
--   $$
--   \Phi(x_k)-\Phi^*\le\Big(\frac{1}{1+\alpha\mu}\Big)^k\Gamma_\alpha(x_0); \tag{4.8}
--   $$
--   3. (Bregman distance to the solution set) for every $k\ge0$,
--   $$
--   \inf_{z\in\mathcal X}D_w(z,x_k)\le\alpha\,\Gamma_\alpha(x_0)\Big(\frac{1}{1+\alpha\mu}\Big)^{k+1}; \tag{4.9}
--   $$
--   4. if $\alpha=\alpha_0$, then for every $k\ge0$, with the condition number $Q:=L/\mu$,
--   $$
--   \Gamma_{\alpha_0}(x_k)\le\Big(1-\frac{1}{[\ell(\tau+1)Q+1](\tau+1)}\Big)^k\Gamma_{\alpha_0}(x_0). \tag{4.10}
--   $$
--
--   This is the main result of the paper: the proximal-like incremental aggregated gradient method, with arbitrary bounded delays and Bregman proximal terms, converges globally linearly under the Bregman distance growth condition, without strong convexity of the objective and without Lipschitz continuity of the gradients. It covers the IAG, PIAG and NoLips methods as special cases.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - generalization: τ the smallest upper bound for all delayed indexes (A0), B4 required when it is positive → τ any natural number with τ_k^n ≤ τ for all k, n; the B4 inequality required when τ > 0; reason: the smallest bound is an instance, for which the hypotheses are exactly the paper’s; the proof only uses τ_k^n ≤ τ
--   - encoding: ℓ monotonically increasing with ℓ(1) = 1 (introduced by B4 when τ > 0; ℓ(τ+1) = ℓ(1) = 1 when τ = 0) → ℓ : ℕ → ℝ with Monotone ℓ and ℓ 1 = 1 always; reason: when τ = 0 only ℓ(1) = 1 enters; ℓ(0) is never read and a monotone ℓ on the positive integers extends by ℓ(0) := ℓ(1)
--   - reading: ∅ ≠ J_k ⊆ J_k (p.8) → J k : Finset (Fin N) with (J k).Nonempty, I_k = (J k)ᶜ; reason: misprint for J_k ⊆ N = {1, …, N}; components indexed by Fin N
--   - encoding: x_k = x_0 for k < 0; Σ_{j=k−τ}^k with negative j → truncated ℕ subtraction k − τ_k^j and Finset.Icc (k − τ) k; reason: same iterates; the omitted negative-index terms are D_w(x_0, x_0) = 0
--   - encoding: L := max_{k≥0} Σ_{j∈J_k} L_j → Lmax Lc J := ⨆ k, Σ_{j ∈ J k} Lc j (real supremum); reason: the family takes finitely many values, so the supremum is the maximum
--   - encoding: x_{k+1} = arg min_{x∈Q} Φ_k(x) → IsPLIAGSeq: x_{k+1} ∈ Q is a minimizer of Φ_k over Q = closure (edom w); reason: under the theorem hypotheses the minimizer is unique (Proposition 3.1 with B2), so the runs are the same
--   - encoding: condition number Q := L/μ → Lmax Lc J / μ (the letter Q names the constraint set); reason: notation only
--   - encoding: functions ℝ^d → (−∞, ∞], convex in the extended sense → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin d) → EReal, convexity as convexity of the epigraph; reason: Lean convention; same instances
--   - encoding: D_w(y, x) defined for y ∈ dom w, x ∈ int dom w → bregman w y x in EReal, equal to +∞ for y ∉ dom w; reason: the paper extended arithmetic; identical on dom w, and it makes inf over X and (3.1) mean what the page says
--   - encoding: ∇w, ∇f_j on int dom w → gradient of the real functions (w ·).toReal, (f_j ·).toReal; reason: w and f_j are finite on the open set int dom w, so the gradients coincide
--   - encoding: B4 for every finite sequence {v_1, …, v_k} in int dom w → B4 for every v : ℕ → ℝ^d with all terms in int dom w; reason: equivalent: a finite sequence extends by repeating its last term, and each inequality reads only v_j, …, v_k
-- source:
--   Zhang, Dai, Guo, Peng, Proximal-Like Incremental Aggregated Gradient Method with Linear Convergence under Bregman Distance Growth Conditions, arXiv:1711.01136v3, Theorem 4.2, p.12 (proof pp.25–26)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_TensorAHPE_IsProperClosedConvex
import Definitions.Def_AubinLipschitz_effDom
import Definitions.Def_PLIAG_IsLegendre
import Definitions.Def_PLIAG_bregman
import Definitions.Def_PLIAG_Phi
import Definitions.Def_PLIAG_PhiStar
import Definitions.Def_PLIAG_optSet
import Definitions.Def_PLIAG_AssumptionB1
import Definitions.Def_PLIAG_AssumptionB2
import Definitions.Def_PLIAG_AssumptionB3
import Definitions.Def_PLIAG_AssumptionB4
import Definitions.Def_PLIAG_IsPLIAGSeq
import Definitions.Def_PLIAG_Lmax
import Definitions.Def_PLIAG_alpha0
import Definitions.Def_PLIAG_Gamma

namespace PLIAG

/-- **Theorem 4.2 (Linear convergence using a growth condition)** (Zhang–Dai–Guo–Peng,
arXiv:1711.01136v3, p.12). Let `L := max_k Σ_{j ∈ J_k} L_j`. Under assumptions B1–B4 (and the
standing assumptions: `h` proper lsc convex, `w` Legendre with `Q = cl dom w`, `X` nonempty and
compact, delays bounded by `τ`), for the PLIAG method with constant step
`0 < α ≤ α_0 := ((1 + (μ/L)·1/ℓ(τ+1))^{1/(τ+1)} − 1)/μ` (4.5) and `Γ_α` of (4.6):
* (4.7) `Γ_α(x_k) ≤ (1/(1+αμ))^k Γ_α(x_0)` for all `k ≥ 0`;
* (4.8) `Φ(x_k) − Φ* ≤ (1/(1+αμ))^k Γ_α(x_0)` for all `k ≥ 0`;
* (4.9) `inf_{z ∈ X} D_w(z, x_k) ≤ α Γ_α(x_0) (1/(1+αμ))^{k+1}` for all `k ≥ 0`;
* (4.10) if `α = α_0`, `Γ_{α_0}(x_k) ≤ (1 − 1/([ℓ(τ+1)κ + 1](τ+1)))^k Γ_{α_0}(x_0)` for all
  `k ≥ 0`, with `κ := L/μ` (the paper's condition number `Q`).

**Formalization Note.** `ℝ^d = EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin d)`; extended values are `EReal`
(`D_w = +∞` off `dom w`); `Q = closure (AubinLipschitz.effDom w)`; components indexed by `Fin N`; `τ` is any upper
bound of the delays (the paper's smallest bound is an instance); `ℓ` is `Monotone` with `ℓ 1 = 1`,
and the B4 inequality is required only when `τ > 0`; the paper's condition number `Q = L/μ` is
written `Lmax Lc J / μ`. -/
theorem theorem_4_2 {d N : ℕ} (w : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin d) → EReal)
    (f : Fin N → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin d) → EReal) (h : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin d) → EReal)
    (Lc : Fin N → ℝ) (ℓ : ℕ → ℝ) (τ : ℕ) (J : ℕ → Finset (Fin N)) (τd : ℕ → Fin N → ℕ)
    (μ α : ℝ) (x : ℕ → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin d))
    (hw : IsLegendre w) (hh : TensorAHPE.IsProperClosedConvex h)
    (hXne : (optSet w f h).Nonempty) (hXc : IsCompact (optSet w f h))
    (hJ : ∀ k, (J k).Nonempty) (hA0 : ∀ k n, τd k n ≤ τ)
    (hB1 : AssumptionB1 w f Lc) (hB2 : AssumptionB2 w h) (hB3 : AssumptionB3 w f h μ)
    (hℓm : Monotone ℓ) (hℓ1 : ℓ 1 = 1) (hB4 : 0 < τ → AssumptionB4 w ℓ)
    (hα : 0 < α) (hαle : α ≤ alpha0 μ (Lmax Lc J) ℓ τ)
    (hx : IsPLIAGSeq w f h J τd α x) :
    (∀ k : ℕ, Gamma w f h α (x k) ≤
        (((1 / (1 + α * μ)) ^ k : ℝ) : EReal) * Gamma w f h α (x 0)) ∧
    (∀ k : ℕ, Phi f h (x k) - PhiStar w f h ≤
        (((1 / (1 + α * μ)) ^ k : ℝ) : EReal) * Gamma w f h α (x 0)) ∧
    (∀ k : ℕ, (⨅ z ∈ optSet w f h, bregman w z (x k)) ≤
        (α : EReal) * Gamma w f h α (x 0) * (((1 / (1 + α * μ)) ^ (k + 1) : ℝ) : EReal)) ∧
    (α = alpha0 μ (Lmax Lc J) ℓ τ → ∀ k : ℕ, Gamma w f h α (x k) ≤
        (((1 - 1 / ((ℓ (τ + 1) * (Lmax Lc J / μ) + 1) * ((τ : ℝ) + 1))) ^ k : ℝ) : EReal) *
          Gamma w f h α (x 0)) := by sorry

end PLIAG
